{"name":"Seine","hex":"#8b8074","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Seine","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A river in northern France that flows through Paris for about 772 km (480 mi) to the English Channel near Le Havre.","A former department of France, the capital city of which was Paris."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Seine"}],"entries":[{"title":"Seine","blocks":[{"text":"The Seine is a 777-kilometre-long (483 mi) river in northern France. Its drainage basin is in the Paris Basin covering most of northern France. It rises at Source-Seine, 30 kilometres (19 mi) northwest of Dijon in northeastern France in the Langres plateau, flowing through Paris and into the English Channel at Le Havre. It is navigable by ocean-going vessels as far as Rouen, 120 kilometres (75 mi) from the sea. Over 60 percent of its length, as far as Burgundy, is negotiable by large barges and most tour boats, and nearly its whole length is available for recreational boating; excursion boats offer sightseeing tours of the river banks in the capital city, Paris."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ed/Bercy%2C_Paris_01.jpg/330px-Bercy%2C_Paris_01.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Seine"},{"title":"Seine (Van Gogh series)","blocks":[{"text":"Seine (paintings) is the subject and location of paintings that Vincent van Gogh made in 1887. The Seine has been an integral part of Parisian life for centuries for commerce, travel and entertainment. Here van Gogh primarily captures the respite and relief from city life found in nature."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b1/Van_Gogh_-_Angler_und_Boote_an_der_Pont_de_Clichy.jpeg/330px-Van_Gogh_-_Angler_und_Boote_an_der_Pont_de_Clichy.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Seine_(Van_Gogh_series)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ca/Bassin_Seine.png/500px-Bassin_Seine.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ca/Bassin_Seine.png/1280px-Bassin_Seine.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ca/Bassin_Seine.png/500px-Bassin_Seine.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABassin_Seine.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1f/2007_Paris_Seine.jpg/500px-2007_Paris_Seine.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1f/2007_Paris_Seine.jpg/1280px-2007_Paris_Seine.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1f/2007_Paris_Seine.jpg/500px-2007_Paris_Seine.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"View over the Seine in Paris, Pont des Invalides in the foreground, Eiffel tower in the background","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3A2007_Paris_Seine.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5d/Source_Seine.jpg/330px-Source_Seine.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5d/Source_Seine.jpg/330px-Source_Seine.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The source of the Seine","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASource_Seine.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a9/Chatillon-sur-Seine_-_Mus%C3%A9e_du_Pays_chatillonnais_-_Crat%C3%A8re_de_Vix_-_012_%28cropped%29.jpg/500px-Chatillon-sur-Seine_-_Mus